[2026-03-16T00:25:59.488Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9X1S4X1BN6M2dvHwDVLAB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Skill\n     2→\n     3→The skill documents used to build the app have directives sections for requirements that must\n     4→be adhered to when performing that stage of development. During this stage you will systematically\n     5→go through the entire app and check that its behavior is following all directives.\n     6→\n     7→## Unpack Subtasks\n     8→\n     9→Read `docs/tests.md` to understand the existing application structure. Add ALL page tasks\n    10→and the backend task in a single `add-task` call. Write out every page explicitly — do not\n    11→use a loop or script:\n    12→\n    13→```bash\n    14→npx tsx /repo/scripts/add-task.ts <<'EOF'\n    15→[\n    16→  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n    17→    \"CheckTestSpec<PageName>: Check testSpec.md directive violations in <PageName> test entries\",\n    18→    \"CheckComponents<PageName>: Check writeApp.md directive violations in <PageName> components\",\n    19→    \"CheckTests<PageName>: Check writeTests.md directive violations in <PageName> tests\"\n    20→  ]},\n    21→  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n    22→    \"CheckBackend: Check writeApp.md directive violations in all backend functions\"\n    23→  ]}\n    24→]\n    25→EOF\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→## Checking for violations\n    29→\n    30→During each checking subtask you need to read the skill document and all the directives,\n    31→and then go through all the documentation / code you are checking to look for violations of those directives.\n    32→You must do this systematically and announce each entry name / file you are checking.\n    33→\n    34→For any violations you find, add a fix task using `add-task`. Do not fix them immediately.\n    35→\n    36→Example:\n    37→```bash\n    38→npx tsx /repo/scripts/add-task.ts <<'EOF'\n    39→[{ \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n    40→  \"FixViolation: Fix <violation description>\",\n    41→  \"RunTests: Run tests/<affected-spec>.spec.ts to verify fix\",\n    42→  \"DocumentFix: Document the fix\"\n    43→]}]\n    44→EOF\n    45→```\n    46→\n    47→## Fixing violations\n    48→\n    49→Fix the relevant documentation / code to make sure it is not violating the directives.\n    50→Make sure to update anything else affected by the changes you are making, in `docs/tests.md`, the app code,\n    51→and playwright tests.\n    52→\n    53→## Running tests\n    54→\n    55→Before running any tests, kill stale processes that may be holding ports:\n    56→```bash\n    57→pkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null; pkill -f \"vite\" 2>/dev/null; sleep 1\n    58→```\n    59→Stale `netlify dev` or `node` processes from prior runs are a frequent cause of test failures.\n    60→\n    61→Make sure all tests pass. Read `skills/tasks/build/testing.md` to understand how to run tests and debug failures.\n    62→\n    63→## Tips\n    64→\n    65→- Group related fix subtasks into a single FixViolation subtask when they share the same root cause\n    66→  (e.g. \"FixViolationMissingTestIds\" for all modals missing data-testid attributes).\n    67→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970","uuid":"bc3cca0b-e1d2-40f7-89b4-7bd1f3573bef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md","content":"# Skill\n\nThe skill documents used to build the app have directives sections for requirements that must\nbe adhered to when performing that stage of development. During this stage you will systematically\ngo through the entire app and check that its behavior is following all directives.\n\n## Unpack Subtasks\n\nRead `docs/tests.md` to understand the existing application structure. Add ALL page tasks\nand the backend task in a single `add-task` call. Write out every page explicitly — do not\nuse a loop or script:\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx /repo/scripts/add-task.ts <<'EOF'\n[\n  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n    \"CheckTestSpec<PageName>: Check testSpec.md directive violations in <PageName> test entries\",\n    \"CheckComponents<PageName>: Check writeApp.md directive violations in <PageName> components\",\n    \"CheckTests<PageName>: Check writeTests.md directive violations in <PageName> tests\"\n  ]},\n  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n    \"CheckBackend: Check writeApp.md directive violations in all backend functions\"\n  ]}\n]\nEOF\n```\n\n## Checking for violations\n\nDuring each checking subtask you need to read the skill document and all the directives,\nand then go through all the documentation / code you are checking to look for violations of those directives.\nYou must do this systematically and announce each entry name / file you are checking.\n\nFor any violations you find, add a fix task using `add-task`. Do not fix them immediately.\n\nExample:\n```bash\nnpx tsx /repo/scripts/add-task.ts <<'EOF'\n[{ \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\", \"app\": \"<AppName>\", \"subtasks\": [\n  \"FixViolation: Fix <violation description>\",\n  \"RunTests: Run tests/<affected-spec>.spec.ts to verify fix\",\n  \"DocumentFix: Document the fix\"\n]}]\nEOF\n```\n\n## Fixing violations\n\nFix the relevant documentation / code to make sure it is not violating the directives.\nMake sure to update anything else affected by the changes you are making, in `docs/tests.md`, the app code,\nand playwright tests.\n\n## Running tests\n\nBefore running any tests, kill stale processes that may be holding ports:\n```bash\npkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null; pkill -f \"vite\" 2>/dev/null; sleep 1\n```\nStale `netlify dev` or `node` processes from prior runs are a frequent cause of test failures.\n\nMake sure all tests pass. Read `skills/tasks/build/testing.md` to understand how to run tests and debug failures.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Group related fix subtasks into a single FixViolation subtask when they share the same root cause\n  (e.g. \"FixViolationMissingTestIds\" for all modals missing data-testid attributes).\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
