ng inputs directly. For the price breakdown tests, I need to interact with the calendar to change dates and verify the breakdown updates accordingly. And for the reserve button test, I'll follow the same pattern of using the calendar to set dates before attempting to book. I need to focus on the core violation: the tests are written for native date inputs, but the component uses a custom calendar instead. For the \"past dates\" test, I should check that past date buttons have the disabled attribute rather than looking for a `min` attribute. The \"check-out after check-in\" test needs to verify the actual behavior in `handleSelectDate` where selecting an earlier date resets the selection. For the repeated use test, I'll need to adjust how I'm checking the selected dates since `toHaveValue` won't work with the custom calendar implementation.\n\nSince the check-in and check-out are now `<p>` elements, I should use `toContainText` with the formatted date output. The guest selector uses `data-value` attributes which I can verify with `toHaveAttribute`. I'll need to add test IDs to the calendar navigation buttons and create a helper function to select dates through the calendar interface, then systematically update each test that currently relies on `.fill()` to work with the custom calendar instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12754,"cache_read_input_tokens":19770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970","uuid":"05ced297-b8c6-44e8-a728-9748260b12f2"}
