[2026-03-16T00:48:43.174Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QCdsM99qExxV6MSgYHMDTo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The query SUCCEEDS (result count: 1)! The error happens AFTER the query. The ECONNREFUSED is from something in the netlify dev infrastructure, not from the neon driver.\n\nLooking at the error flow:\n1. Properties function queries the database - SUCCESS (result count: 1)\n2. The function tries to return the Response\n3. Something in the netlify dev infrastructure fails with ECONNREFUSED\n\nThe issue is in how netlify dev handles the Response object. Since the function uses V2 API (returns a `Response` object), netlify dev tries to handle this as a streaming response through a Worker thread. The Worker thread creates a local server to stream the response body back to the parent, and the parent tries to connect to it.\n\n\nThe worker code checks if the invocation result has a streaming body and creates a local server with a random port, while the parent process tries to connect to that port. But our function doesn't actually stream—it returns a regular Response with JSON—so either the V2 handler is incorrectly treating it as a stream, or something's converting the Response into a streaming format when it shouldn't be. The issue is that the function is written in V2 format (using Request/Response) but the runtime detection logic is checking for `runtimeAPIVersion === 2` to decide whether to invoke it through the Worker path or directly—and if that check fails, it falls back to `invokeFunctionDirectly`, which uses lambda-local that expects the old V1 format with `{ statusCode, body, headers }` objects instead of Response objects. The `lambdaEvent` returned from `lambdaLocal.execute()` might be wrapping the `Response` object, and the `body` property could be a `ReadableStream` that the `isStream()` check detects, triggering the worker to try piping it—but Node.js streams and web `ReadableStream` aren't compatible. I should check if all the functions in the app are using V2 format and returning `Response` objects, which might explain why this pattern is failing across the board.\n\nActually, if this were a fundamental V2 incompatibility with netlify dev, every API call would fail, not just the property detail endpoint. The test shows the home page loads with the navbar visible, so at least some requests are working. The properties list API might also be failing silently, leaving the home page empty, while the property detail page explicitly shows the 500 error. Let me look at what's actually rendering on the home page to see if the listings are there or if that API call failed too. The rejection handler might not be setting the error state correctly if the payload is missing, which would cause the component to show \"Property not found\" instead of the actual error. The real issue is that the Netlify dev function runtime has a bug with V2 functions returning Response objects with ReadableStream bodies—it tries to pipe the stream through a local server and fails. I should try converting the response body to a string or Buffer before returning, or switch back to the V1 function format.\n\nNow I'm wondering if this is specific to the netlify-cli version or if there's an architecture issue since the machine is running on linux-arm64.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":986,"cache_read_input_tokens":123776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":986,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970","uuid":"80aee78e-0bdf-4356-9f01-734097c4a6f3"}
