[2026-03-16T01:06:53.890Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PxgcY5hfEhjBPnnoKnM2DN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ALL property-detail-related tests fail. The tests that passed were for different pages (trips/bookings, etc.) that don't navigate to property detail pages. So the property detail API endpoint is consistently broken.\n\nLet me think about this. The property list endpoint works (tests for property grid may have issues too but let me check). The bookings/auth/trips tests pass because they use different API endpoints.\n\nThe key question: why does `/api/properties/<uuid>` return a 404 with \"Property not found\"?\n\nLooking at the properties function code again:\n```typescript\nconst url = new URL(request.url)\nconst segments = url.pathname.split('/').filter(Boolean)\n\n\n```\n\nI'm extracting the property ID from the URL path segments. In a V2 function running in netlify dev, the redirect rule maps `/api/*` to `/.netlify/functions/:splat`, so the function receives `/.netlify/functions/properties/<uuid>` instead of the original `/api/properties/<uuid>`. When the redirect applies, `:splat` captures `properties/<uuid>`, which means the function's `request.url` contains the rewritten path, not the original API path. actually, netlify dev handles this differently. When you have a V2 function, the function name is `properties` and the request URL sent to it might be different. Let me think...\n\nIn netlify dev, when a request comes in for `/api/properties/<uuid>`:\n1. The redirect rule maps it to `/.netlify/functions/properties/<uuid>`\n2. Netlify dev sees this is a function call for the `properties` function\n3. It extracts the function name (`properties`) and calls the function\n4. For V2 functions, the request URL might be different from what we expect\n\nThe bootstrap wraps the V2 function in a V1 lambda handler that receives an event with the path, raw URL, and headers, then 