[2026-03-16T01:10:07.889Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017Jj7rbjUDc72bbL8aqTEBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Lambda-local loads streaming.js at the top level when imported:```javascript\nrequire(\"./lib/streaming.js\");\n```\n\nThis sets `global.awslambda`. But in the worker.js:```javascript\nimport lambdaLocal from 'lambda-local'\n// ...\nconst lambdaFunc = await import(entryFilePath)\n```\n\nThe `import lambdaLocal from 'lambda-local'` is at the top of the file (static import). The `import(entryFilePath)` is a dynamic import. Static imports execute before any module code runs. But `lambda-local` uses CommonJS (`require`), and `global.awslambda` is set when `streaming.js` is required by `lambdalocal.js`.\n\n\nWhen the worker imports lambda-local as an ESM module, the CommonJS code executes immediately and sets `global.awslambda` before the dynamic import of the entry file happens. This means the entry point's bootstrap code can successfully call `awslambda.streamifyResponse()` since the global is already available.\n\nThe handler gets wrapped in streamifyResponse and returns a PassThrough stream, which the worker correctly identifies as a stream and pipes through a TCP server for the parent to consume. But the actual error is ECONNREFUSED on a random port, which suggests the TCP server itself might not be starting properly or the parent is trying to connect before it's ready. The response gets sent back to the client, but the ECONNREFUSED error suggests the parent can't connect to the TCP server the worker created—either the worker exits too quickly or the server setup fails. Though wait, the Neon query actually succeeds and the error happens during response delivery, not the query itself. Let me step back and consider whether the streaming mechanism is even the problem, or if there's a simpler V1-style response approach that would avoid this complexity altogether.\n\nActually, the function already returns a standard Response object, but the V2 bootstrap automatically converts it to streaming format regardless. Converting to V1 format would bypass streaming entirely, but that's a massive change since all V2 functions would need conversion. Let me explore other options instead.\n\nI should try clearing the `.netlify/functions-serve/` cache to force a fresh build—the stale cache might be the culprit. Before that, let me check whether the earlier passing test runs (13, 16, 18) actually used V2 functions or if they relied on V1 format instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":105243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970","uuid":"d871e3e7-efc9-44be-8572-9a3f2152e208"}
