[2026-03-16T01:34:57.609Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user assigned two subtasks from a checkDirectives maintenance skill:\n   - **FixViolation**: BookingCard tests assume native date inputs (`fill`, `toHaveAttribute type=date`, `toHaveValue`) but the component uses a custom calendar with `<p>` elements for `booking-checkin` and `booking-checkout`. Tests need to be rewritten to interact with the custom calendar UI. **(COMPLETED in previous session)**\n   - **RunTests**: Run `tests/booking-card.spec.ts` to verify the fix. **(COMPLETED - all 16 tests pass)**\n   \n   The user expects `<DONE>` to be output upon completion of both subtasks.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - AirbnbClone app in `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/`\n   - Playwright tests with Replay browser recording\n   - Custom calendar component (not native `<input type=\"date\">`)\n   - Netlify Functions V2 format (export default + Response objects)\n   - Neon serverless PostgreSQL driver (`@neondatabase/serverless`)\n   - ZISI (zip-it-and-ship-it) function bundler with `runtimeAPIVersion: 2`\n   - netlify-cli v24.2.0 with bundled function runtime\n   - Lambda response streaming via `awslambda.streamifyResponse()` polyfill in `lambda-local`\n   - Worker threads for V2 function execution with TCP streaming for response bodies\n   - Test script creates ephemeral Neon branches for test isolation\n   - `PATH=/tmp/fake-deno:$PATH` trick to prevent netlify dev from using Deno\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/booking-card.spec.ts`** (modified)\n     - Main test file being fixed. All 16 tests now pass.\n     - Key test changes in this session:\n     ```typescript\n     // Test 1: \"Booking card displays price per night\" - fixed to check both states\n     test('Booking card displays price per night', async ({ page }) => {\n       await page.goto(`/properties/${PROPERTY_LOFT}`)\n       const card = page.getByTestId('booking-card')\n       await expect(card).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })\n       // Without dates selected, shows \"Add dates for prices\"\n       await expect(card).toContainText('Add dates for prices')\n       // After selecting dates, shows \"$150 / night\"\n       await selectDatesViaCalendar(page, '2026-07-10', '2026-07-13')\n       await expect(card).toContainText('$150')\n       await expect(card).toContainText('night')\n     })\n     ```\n     ```typescript\n     // Test 14: \"Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\" - rewritten to verify disabled dates\n     test('Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates', async ({ page }) => {\n       test.slow()\n       await loginAs(page, GUEST_EMAIL)\n       await page.goto('/properties/b2222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222')\n       const card = page.getByTestId('booking-card')\n       await expect(card).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })\n       await openCalendarIfNeeded(page)\n       const aprDay = page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-03')\n       for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\n         if (await aprDay.isVisible().catch(() => false)) break\n         await page.getByTestId('calendar-next-month').click()\n       }\n       // Booked dates (April 1-6) should be disabled in the calendar\n       await expect(page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-01')).toBeDisabled()\n       await expect(page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-03')).toBeDisabled()\n       await expect(page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-06')).toBeDisabled()\n       // Dates outside the booking should be enabled\n       await expect(page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-08')).toBeEnabled()\n       await expect(page.getByTestId('calendar-day-2026-04-10')).toBeEnabled()\n     })\n     ```\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/BookingCard.tsx`** (modified)\n     - Fixed date normalization bug in booked ranges fetch:\n     ```typescript\n     useEffect(() => {\n       fetch(`/api/bookings?property_id=${property.id}`)\n         .then((r) => r.json())\n         .then((data) => {\n           if (Array.isArray(data)) {\n             setBookedRanges(data.map((b: { check_in: string; check_out: string }) => ({\n               check_in: b.check_in.slice(0, 10),\n               check_out: b.check_out.slice(0, 10),\n             })))\n           }\n         })\n         .catch(() => {})\n     }, [property.id])\n     ```\n     - Also had `data-testid=\"calendar-prev-month\"` and `data-testid=\"calendar-next-month\"` added in previous session\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`** (reverted)\n     - Reverted debug code back to original:\n     ```typescript\n     import { neon } from '@neondatabase/serverless'\n     export function getSql() {\n       return neon(process.env.DATABASE_URL!)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/netlify/functions/properties.ts`** (reverted)\n     - Reverted debug try/catch and console.log statements back to clean query code\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/node_modules/netlify-cli/dist/lib/functions/runtimes/js/worker.js`** (patched - NOT git tracked)\n     - **CRITICAL FIX**: This is the actual worker file used by netlify-cli (not the one in `@netlify/functions-dev`)\n     - Replaced TCP streaming with buffered string consumption:\n     ```javascript\n     import process from 'process';\n     import { isMainThread, workerData, parentPort } from 'worker_threads';\n     import { isStream } from 'is-stream';\n     import lambdaLocal from 'lambda-local';\n     import sourceMapSupport from 'source-map-support';\n     if (isMainThread) {\n         throw new Error(`Do not import \"${import.meta.url}\" in the main thread.`);\n     }\n     sourceMapSupport.install();\n     lambdaLocal.getLogger().level = 'alert';\n     const { clientContext, entryFilePath, environment = {}, event, timeoutMs } = workerData;\n     for (const key in environment) {\n         process.env[key] = environment[key];\n     }\n     const lambdaFunc = await import(entryFilePath);\n     const lambdaEvent = await lambdaLocal.execute({\n         clientContext, event, lambdaFunc, region: 'dev', timeoutMs, verboseLevel: 3,\n     });\n     // If the body is a stream, consume it fully into a string.\n     // This avoids the TCP streaming approach which has race conditions in dev.\n     if (lambdaEvent != null && isStream(lambdaEvent.body)) {\n         const body = lambdaEvent.body;\n         const chunks = [];\n         await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n             body.on('data', (chunk) => chunks.push(chunk));\n             body.on('end', () => resolve(undefined));\n             body.on('error', reject);\n             body.resume();\n         });\n         lambdaEvent.body = Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf-8');\n     }\n     if (lambdaEvent == null) {\n         parentPort?.postMessage(lambdaEvent);\n     } else {\n         const message = { ...lambdaEvent };\n         parentPort?.postMessage(message);\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/node_modules/netlify-cli/dist/lib/functions/runtimes/js/index.js`** (read only)\n     - The parent-side code that creates workers and handles streaming responses\n     - When `result.streamPort` is set, parent tries `createConnection({ port: result.streamPort, host: 'localhost' })` - this was failing with ECONNREFUSED\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/scripts/test.ts`** (read only)\n     - Test runner: creates ephemeral Neon branches, seeds DB, writes DATABASE_URL to .env, runs Playwright\n\n   - **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/playwright.config.ts`** (read only)\n     - webServer command: `PATH=/tmp/fake-deno:$PATH npx netlify dev --offline --port 8888 --functions ./netlify/functions`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **ECONNREFUSED on random localhost ports (e.g., 127.0.0.1:37065)**:\n     - Root cause: V2 functions use `awslambda.streamifyResponse()` (polyfilled by lambda-local's streaming.js). The function result body is a `StreamingBody` (PassThrough stream). The worker creates a TCP server to stream the body back to the parent. But the parent's `createConnection()` gets ECONNREFUSED - the TCP server is already gone by the time the parent connects.\n     - Key discovery: netlify-cli has TWO copies of worker.js. The one at `node_modules/netlify-cli/node_modules/@netlify/functions-dev/dist/worker.js` is NOT used. The actual one is at `node_modules/netlify-cli/dist/lib/functions/runtimes/js/worker.js`.\n     - Fix: Patched the correct worker.js to consume the stream body into a string buffer instead of using TCP streaming. This eliminates the race condition.\n     - **This fix is in node_modules and will be lost on `npm install`**\n\n   - **\"Add dates for prices\" vs \"$150/night\"**:\n     - Test expected `$150` visible in booking card, but component only shows price when dates are selected\n     - Fix: Updated test to first verify \"Add dates for prices\" text, then select dates via calendar before checking \"$150\"\n\n   - **Calendar disables booked dates (can't click disabled dates)**:\n     - Test tried to click on `calendar-day-2026-04-02` which was disabled due to existing booking\n     - Fix: Rewrote \"Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\" test to verify that booked dates ARE disabled in the calendar instead of trying to submit overlapping dates\n\n   - **Date format mismatch in BookingCard**:\n     - API returns dates as `\"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\"` (full ISO) but `isDateBooked()` compares against `\"2026-04-01\"` format\n     - String comparison `\"2026-04-01\" >= \"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\"` is `false` because 'T' > end-of-string\n     - Fix: Added `.slice(0, 10)` normalization when setting booked ranges in the useEffect\n\n   - **Intermittent Neon endpoint suspension**:\n     - Neon endpoints have `suspend_timeout_seconds: 60` - they suspend after inactivity\n     - Caused some test runs to have intermittent failures (test-run-89: only 3 passed)\n     - Resolution: Retrying usually succeeds (test-run-90: all 16 passed)\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **SOLVED**: Identified the root cause of the pre-existing netlify dev V2 function failure - streaming TCP race condition in worker thread\n   - **SOLVED**: Found the CORRECT worker.js file (in netlify-cli/dist/, not in @netlify/functions-dev/dist/)\n   - **SOLVED**: Fixed BookingCard date format bug causing booked date blocking to not work\n   - **SOLVED**: Fixed test assertions to match actual component behavior\n   - **SOLVED**: All 16 booking-card tests now pass\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial context continuation message with summary of previous session work, asking to continue from where left off\n   - Summary request message (current)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Output `<DONE>` to signal completion of both subtasks (FixViolation and RunTests)\n   - Note: The worker.js fix in node_modules is not persistent. If `npm install` is run, it will be lost. This should be addressed in future tasks.\n   - Cleanup of leftover Neon branches (br-dry-resonance-a6kzj4lk, br-patient-morning-a6iw50s3) - attempted but auth failed with curl\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Both subtasks are COMPLETED:\n   - **FixViolation**: Tests rewritten to use custom calendar UI ✅\n   - **RunTests**: All 16 tests pass ✅ (test-run-90: `16 passed (38.0s)`)\n   \n   `npm run check` passes. The final state:\n   - `booking-card.spec.ts` - fully rewritten with custom calendar helpers\n   - `BookingCard.tsx` - date normalization fix + calendar test IDs\n   - `db.ts` and `properties.ts` - reverted to clean state\n   - Worker.js patched in node_modules (not git tracked)\n   - `.env` restored to just `NEON_PROJECT_ID=muddy-art-91639904`\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Output `<DONE>` to signal completion of both subtasks. The user's original instruction states: \"When you have completed ALL subtasks in your task, output `<DONE>` to signal completion.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/agent/.claude/projects/-repo/bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd78e25b-7fce-4bae-a91a-1f392b40d970","uuid":"b2bb4d51-d5b6-4ba6-8909-009ffbd1ccb0","isSynthetic":true}
